{"type":"text","timestamp":1794528210653,"sessionID":"ses_e2dcb3158ffe0I0x9310AmKw3h","part":{"id":"prt_1d23761eb001LZZ2ELNyMUTI0B","sessionID":"ses_e2dcb3158ffe0I0x9310AmKw3h","messageID":"msg_1d2375b5c00176ZX9A2X6cGkQC","type":"text","text":"T033 is done. Both `command-spec-kit-plan` occurrences in the test now read `command-speckit-plan`.\n\n**File written**\n\n`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/scorer/same-owner-ambiguity.vitest.ts`, lines 19 and 23 only. Diff:\n\n```diff\n-    (entry) => entry.id === 'command-spec-kit-plan' && entry.ownerSkill,\n+    (entry) => entry.id === 'command-speckit-plan' && entry.ownerSkill,\n\n-      'no owning skill is recorded for command-spec-kit-plan in the bridge data; '\n+      'no owning skill is recorded for command-speckit-plan in the bridge data; '\n```\n\n**Verify**\n\n```\n$ rg -c \"command-spec-kit-\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/scorer/same-owner-ambiguity.vitest.ts\n(no output)\nVERIFY_EXIT:1\n```\n\n`rg` exits 1 on no match, so the required \"prints nothing\" holds. Positive control on the same file prints the two new ids at lines 19 and 23, which shows the pattern was exercised rather than skipped.\n\n**Not done, and why**\n\nThe checkbox in `tasks.md` is untouched, as instructed. I did not run the test file: T033 names only the `rg` verify, and the generated bridge data still carries the old id (`command-spec-kit-plan` appears 6 times in `command-bridges.generated.json`, no `command-speckit-plan` yet), so the fixture would throw until T034 runs `node $D`. That is observed, not inferred, and it is the one residual dependency for this task.\n\nNothing is the operator's to do. The orchestrator's next step is T034's regeneration, then T027 to T033 can be considered as a wave.","time":{"start":1794528207339,"end":1794528210653}}}
